"dwc_country_replaced","idigbio_isocountrycode_added","gbif_vernacularname_added","gbif_taxon_corrected","dwc_continent_added"],"locality":"mobile","recordset":"a3b77120-3770-46dd-ba47-6941eff848b3","occurrenceid":"d3a1fd0b-cf8f-4278-b12d-da8437bb610a","scientificname":"solenopsis richteri","stateprovince":"alabama","uuid":"fb824399-a59a-4084-9caa-c35598e49d4c","taxonid":"5035017","taxonomicstatus":"accepted","catalognumber":"x1172538","basisofrecord":"preservedspecimen","canonicalname":"solenopsis richteri","taxonrank":"species","institutioncode":"tamu"}}],"attribution":[{"uuid":"3a0018d0-9b91-4671-82d2-b635177dace6","itemCount":10,"name":"LACM Entomology Collection","description":"With over 800,000 described species — more than half of all known living organisms — insects are the most diverse group of animals on Earth. The Natural History Museum's entomology collection has more than 5.8 million specimens of insects and spiders. The collection's strength lies in its holdings of specimens of ants, phorid flies, scarab beetles, and moths from North and Central America. Museum scientists conduct world-class research on systematics, studying species and their relationships, the evolution of major groups, and fossil insects in amber. They conduct field work on insect biodiversity at home and in tropical countries. Entomology at the Natural History Museum of Los Angeles County goes back as far as 1913, when the Museum first opened.","logo":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/logo.do?r=lacm_ento","url":"http://www.nhm.org/site/research-collections/entomology https://ipt.vertnet.org/archive.do?r=lacm_ento","emllink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/eml.do?r=lacm_ento","archivelink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/archive.do?r=lacm_ento","contacts":[{"first_name":"William","last_name":"Mertz","role":"Database & Reports Manager","email":"wmertz@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"Giar-Ann","last_name":"Kung","role":"Collections Manager","email":"gkung@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"Weiping","last_name":"Xie","role":"Collections Manager","email":"wxie@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"William","last_name":"Mertz","role":"Database & Reports Manager","email":"wmertz@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"Weiping","last_name":"Xie","role":"Collections Manager","email":"wxie@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"Giar-Ann","last_name":"Kung","role":"Collections Manager","email":"gkung@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Bloom","email":"dbloom@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"William","last_name":"Mertz","role":"Database & Reports Manager","email":"wmertz@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"Weiping","last_name":"Xie","role":"Collections Manager","email":"wxie@nhm.org"},{"first_name":"Giar-Ann","last_name":"Kung","role":"Collections Manager","email":"gkung@nhm.org"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"842a2bb5-d705-4d6c-8401-abf3ca28c05d","totalCount":663448,"hitRatio":0.000015072771340029664},{"uuid":"ff111763-e72d-4f24-8914-b5b2dd94908c","itemCount":4,"name":"New Mexico State Collection of Arthropods","description":"The New Mexico State Collection of Arthropods is located at New Mexico State University in Las Cruces, NM. It currently houses approximately 150,000 arthropod specimens as well as the Merrill Sweet Collection (350,000 specimens). The NMSU Collection primarily is composed of arthropods from the western United States, with an emphasis on the arachnids of the arid Southwest. The goals of the collection include survey of the arthropod fauna of New Mexico and the Southwest, providing reference material for researchers, and providing outreach to our constituents in the state and abroad.","logo":"http://scan-bugs.org/portal/images/collicons/nms.png","url":"http://arthropods.nmsu.edu/","emllink":"https://scan-bugs.org:443/portal/content/dwca/nmsu-nmsu_dwc-a.eml","archivelink":"https://scan-bugs.org:443/portal/content/dwca/nmsu-nmsu_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"scan_noreply@asu.edu"},{"email":"scan_noreply@asu.edu"},{"first_name":"Scott Bundy","email":"cbundy@nmsu.edu"},{"first_name":"Neil"},{"first_name":"Scott Bundy","role":"Collection Manager","email":"cbundy@nmsu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"076c0ff6-65e9-48a5-8e4b-2447936f9a1c","totalCount":107510,"hitRatio":0.000037205841317086785},{"uuid":"8eabbc48-2b30-419d-bd8f-eece9185eca1","itemCount":3,"name":"Mississippi Entomological Museum","description":"The Mississippi Entomological Museum is located in the Department of Entomology and Plant Pathology at Mississippi State University near Starkville, Mississippi. The Mississippi Entomological Museum was formed in 1979, under the leadership of Dr. William H. Cross, to combine several private and institutional collections that were present in the state. The research collection contains more than 1,300,000 pinned specimens, and more than 35,000 are being added annually. The Mississippi Entomological Museum includes collections, beginning in the late 1800's of H. E. Weed, Henry Dietrich, J. M. Langston, R. W. Harned, Gladys Hoke-Lobdell, E. W. Stafford, M. R. Smith, William H. Cross, Leon W. Hepner, Bryant Mather, and Charles Bryson. Exotic material includes taxa from Central and South America, the Seychelles, New Caledonia, and the Fiji Islands. The MacDonald Collection, emphasizing Lepidoptera of Panama, is housed in the Mississippi Entomological Museum as well as the Ross E. Hutchins collection of photographs, which are primarily of insects and other natural history subjects, and the James Solomon collection of wood damage. More information about the collection is available at http://mississippientomologicalmuseum.org.msstate.edu/. For information pertaining to loans, contact the Curator, Terence Schiefer (tschiefer@entomology.msstate.edu).","logo":"http://scan-bugs.org/portal/content/collicon/missa-mem.jpg","url":"http://mississippientomologicalmuseum.org.msstate.edu/","emllink":"https://scan-bugs.org:443/portal/content/dwca/missa-mem_dwc-a.eml","archivelink":"https://scan-bugs.org:443/portal/content/dwca/missa-mem_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"scan_noreply@asu.edu"},{"email":"scan_noreply@asu.edu"},{"first_name":"JoVonn Hill","email":"Jgh4@entomology.msstate.edu"},{"first_name":"Neil"},{"first_name":"JoVonn Hill","role":"Collection Manager","email":"Jgh4@entomology.msstate.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"076c0ff6-65e9-48a5-8e4b-2447936f9a1c","totalCount":334633,"hitRatio":0.000008965045288420449},{"uuid":"32d433aa-9e2b-4ff9-bc55-5c3e30112207","itemCount":1,"name":"Field Museum of Natural History (Zoology) Insect, Arachnid and Myriapod Collection","description":"The Division of Insects’ holdings of worldwide Arthropoda (excluding Crustacea) rank fifth in overall size among North American collections and are of worldwide importance for many groups. The collection presently includes roughly 4.1 million pinned insects plus 8.3 million specimens or lots in alcohol or on microscope slides. In addition, there are over 17,000 partly-sorted “bulk samples” from traps or leaf-litter extractions. The collection receives heavy use by US and international research visitors and borrowers as well as extensive educational use.","logo":"https://fmipt.fieldmuseum.org/ipt/logo.do?r=fmnh_insects","url":"http://fieldmuseum.org/explore/department/zoology/insects/collections","emllink":"https://fmipt.fieldmuseum.org/ipt/eml.do?r=fmnh_insects","archivelink":"https://fmipt.fieldmuseum.org/ipt/archive.do?r=fmnh_insects","contacts":[{"first_name":"Sharon","last_name":"Grant","role":"Technology Liaison to Science","email":"sgrant@fieldmuseum.org"},{"first_name":"Kate","last_name":"Webbink"},{"first_name":"Maureen","last_name":"Turcatel","role":"Collection Manager Insects, Arachnids and Myriapods","email":"mturcatel@fieldmuseum.org"},{"first_name":"Rebekah","last_name":"Shuman","role":"Collection Assistant"},{"first_name":"Sharon","last_name":"Grant","role":"Technology Liaison to Science","email":"sgrant@fieldmuseum.org"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"50ac82da-811d-4440-b1a7-d3a35a8c5f89","totalCount":478932,"hitRatio":0.0000020879790868014667},{"uuid":"a3b77120-3770-46dd-ba47-6941eff848b3","itemCount":1,"name":"Texas A&M University Insect Collection","description":"The Texas A&M University Insect Collection (TAMUIC) is a land-grant-university-based collection of insects and related arthropods whose primary holdings are focused on the regional faunas of the south-central and southwestern United States and the northern neotropics, especially Mexico. As the oldest and largest entomological collection in Texas, the TAMUIC serves research, education and extension missions throughout the state, and particularly supports the diverse activities of the TAMU Department of Entomology. The TAMUIC has grown steadily through the years, especially in the last three decades, to become a major research collection with 2.6+ million curated specimens and holdings of more than 45,000 species. Approximately 10,000 specimens are loaned annually to systematics and biodiversity researchers around the world.","logo":"http://scan-bugs.org/portal/images/collicons/atm.jpg","url":"http://insects.tamu.edu/tamuinsectcollection/","emllink":"https://scan-bugs.org:443/portal/content/dwca/tamu-tamuic_dwc-a.eml","archivelink":"https://scan-bugs.org:443/portal/content/dwca/tamu-tamuic_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"scan_noreply@asu.edu"},{"email":"scan_noreply@asu.edu"},{"first_name":"Karen Wright","email":"kwright@tamu.edu"},{"first_name":"Neil"},{"first_name":"Karen Wright","role":"Collection Manager","email":"kwright@tamu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"076c0ff6-65e9-48a5-8e4b-2447936f9a1c","totalCount":999991,"hitRatio":0.0000010000090000810007},{"uuid":"ded380b5-1ba2-4089-8e0c-0aa1b4140785","itemCount":1,"name":"AntWeb","description":"AntWeb is the world's largest online database of images, specimen records, and natural history information on ants. It is community driven and open to contribution from anyone with specimen records, natural history comments, or images.","logo":"https://monarch.calacademy.org/images/collicons/CAS-ANTWEB.png","url":"http://antweb.org http://ipt.calacademy.org:8080/archive.do?r=antweb","emllink":"http://ipt.calacademy.org:8080/eml.do?r=antweb","archivelink":"http://ipt.calacademy.org:8080/archive.do?r=antweb","contacts":[{"first_name":"Brian L.","last_name":"Fisher","role":"Curator","email":"bfisher@calacademy.org"},{"first_name":"Jon","last_name":"Fong","role":"Programmer","email":"jfong@calacademy.org"},{"first_name":"Brian L. ","last_name":"Fisher","role":"Curator","email":"bfisher@calacademy.org"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY","publisher":"a383e7e0-9fcf-4ffb-9bbf-a42b0d665a7f","totalCount":909185,"hitRatio":0.0000010998861617822556}],"aggs":{"rs":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_doc_count":0,"buckets":[{"key":"3a0018d0-9b91-4671-82d2-b635177dace6","doc_count":10},{"key":"ff111763-e72d-4f24-8914-b5b2dd94908c","doc_count":4},{"key":"8eabbc48-2b30-419d-bd8f-eece9185eca1","doc_count":3},{"key":"32d433aa-9e2b-4ff9-bc55-5c3e30112207","doc_count":1},{"key":"a3b77120-3770-46dd-ba47-6941eff848b3","doc_count":1},{"key":"ded380b5-1ba2-4089-8e0c-0aa1b4140785","doc_count":1}]},"unique_scientific_names":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_doc_count":0,"buckets":[{"key":"solenopsis richteri","doc_count":20}]},"max_dm":{"value":1771955046104,"value_as_string":"2026-02-24T17:44:06.104Z"}}}